  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the rate of cooling of the object is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>For the first case, it can be written, using equation (1) that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>K</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>50</mn><mi>K</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;is the required time for the second case, from equation (1), it can be written that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>K</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>30</mn><mi>K</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Divide equation (2) by equation (3) and solve to calculate the required time.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>50</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>"
